ref 1079 #uuid "ccdc138e-bb95-5aaf-8e12-5fa2bad487bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244002 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186243797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244002 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107031" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244002 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244002 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the set of matrices ${A,B,C},$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nIf the set is linearly dependent, find the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}$ from a non-zero solution of ${x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O,$ where $O$ is the $2\\times 2$ zero-matrix." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244002 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "20f026a9-c929-5f67-a8ba-c0d4cc456de0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244002 #edb/ref 1074 "If the set is linearly dependent, then there exist ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ not all zero such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O.\n$$\n\nOtherwise, if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ the set is linearly independent.\n\nSubstituting the matrices $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{1} \\\\ 0 & -2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{2} & -{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2} & 4{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3} & -4{x}_{3} \\\\ -8{x}_{3} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} & {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3} & -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the corresponding augmented matrix and reduce it to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -8 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd.\nHence, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable.\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the $2$nd equation, we get ${x}_{2}=4{x}_{3}.$ Substitute it into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(4{x}_{3})+4{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=8{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFinally, for any ${x}_{3}\\ne 0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}=\\frac{8{x}_{3}}{4{x}_{3}}=2.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244501 #edb/ref 1080 "-32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244501 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244501 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "145aaf0d-c740-5655-ae4b-ab7ab839b1d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244793 #edb/ref 1080 "40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244793 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244793 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3645011b-7dde